+
+Every code lever merged from the round-1 campaigns sits behind one of these env
+knobs. All default OFF; with every knob off the server takes exactly the
+recipe (recipe-f34e82ba) code paths. Values are read once at import.
+
+  SGLANG_INFX_MONO_GLUE       r1-c1 it8 (= r1-c4 it10): dual-set mamba state commit,
+                              16 B monokernel mailbox spread, verify-graph QSA metadata
+                              skip, fused simulated-accept writes, fused FutureMap stash
+  SGLANG_INFX_SAMPLE_TAIL     r1-c2 it8: eagle_sample greedy verify + simulated accept
+                              in 2 launches (fused_sim_accept.py)
+  SGLANG_INFX_PREFILL_SPLITK  r1-c16 it5: key-split QSA prefill indexer kernel + 2 fewer
+                              host syncs per QSA layer per prefill chunk
+  SGLANG_INFX_DECODE_GROUPED  r1-c16 it6: grouped (per-request) QSA decode indexer kernel
+                              for target verify
+  (integration-r1b)
+  SGLANG_INFX_MONO_ATTN_TASKS r1-c4 it14: verify monokernel QSA attention tail-first task order,
+                              b128 K LDS stores, V^T XOR swizzle, head-pair qsa_merge (bitwise)
+  SGLANG_INFX_HC_PREFETCH     r1-c16 it10: fused HC down/up kernels issue a K group's activation
+                              loads before its MFMAs (bitwise)
+  SGLANG_INFX_STATE_INPLACE   r1-c8 it9: verify monokernel stores the last draft step's SSM state
+                              into the committed slot + one-launch commit/track; mutually
+                              exclusive with MONO_GLUE's dual-set SSM commit (STATE_INPLACE wins)
+  (integration-r2; map in RUN/state/integration_r2.md)
+  SGLANG_INFX_MONO_MOE_SPREAD r2-c1 it4 (r1-deep2 it8 rebased; = r2-c8 it2 = r2-c2 it5): verify + MTP
+                              monokernel MoE gate_up/down tasks wave-major over all CTAs, first down
+                              piece before the mid wait (bitwise). Off = recipe task order.
+  SGLANG_INFX_MONO_OP_MERGE   r2-c4 it8 (r1-deep2 it10 op_merge; r2-c4 had it under MONO_MOE_SPREAD):
